**Known for**: Popular cryptographic algorithms, e.g. Salsa20, ed25519; qmail,
djbdns

**Alias**: djb

Daniel is an well-known and influential cryptographer and former visiting
professor at TU/Eindhoven,[[source]][0] where he has worked with his wife,
Tanja Lange, the chair of the coding theory and cryptology group
there.[[source]](https://cc.win.tue.nl/staff.html)

Daniel and Tanja are associates of
[Jacob Appelbaum]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('appelbaum')) and served
as his PhD advisors.[[source]][1][[source]][2] One of the students under
Bernstein and Lange at TU/e, Henry de Valence, resigned from their PhD program
in 2016 citing patterns of harassment, abuse, and bullying at the hands of
Jacob, Daniel, and Tanja.[[source]][3]

